Falsifies `inter_process_communication::verification::signal_preserves_the_invariant`.

The defect: the pending count is incremented with a plain `+= 1` instead of saturating. It reads
as the obvious way to count, and a count of four billion unreceived signals looks unreachable.

Expected to fail: Kani's arithmetic overflow check on the increment, when `seed` sets `pending`
to `u32::MAX` and no receiver is queued. The one-queue assertion itself still holds; the harness
goes red because `signal` panics in debug builds and wraps the count to zero in release builds,
which loses every counted signal.

diff --git a/crates/inter_process_communication/src/rendezvous.rs b/crates/inter_process_communication/src/rendezvous.rs
index cfd015317..bfe0cf56b 100644
--- a/crates/inter_process_communication/src/rendezvous.rs
+++ b/crates/inter_process_communication/src/rendezvous.rs
@@ -325,7 +325,7 @@ impl<T: Node> Rendezvous<T> {
         if let Some(receiver) = self.receivers.pop_front() {
             Some(receiver)
         } else {
-            self.pending = self.pending.saturating_add(1);
+            self.pending += 1;
             None
         }
     }
